    "explain_requested": false,
    "reasons": [
      "Every input is normalized into TargetSpec before planning.",
      "Scope is deny-by-default: seed targets and explicit --scope rules are the only permitted expansion.",
      "Workflow recon (level 3) and speed Balanced remain independent policy controls.",
      "Target normalization, Scope Guard, and plan compilation always run.",
      "Level 3 with workflow recon selects: {\"custom\":\"rxscan.control.validate\"}, \"host_discovery\", \"port_discovery\".",
      "No port selection supplied; TCP discovery uses the conservative level-derived common-port policy.",
      "Speed policy: speed Balanced -> concurrency 2, retry_limit 2, default_timeout_ms 15000, deterministic baseline (non-adaptive; auto == balanced).",
      "Budgets: max_tasks 1000, max_retries 1000, max_concurrency 4 (effective 2), max_execution_time_ms 60000, max_evidence_bytes 67108864, max_hosts 256.",
      "Host discovery policy: discovery lightweight level 3: icmp on (x2, 1000ms), tcp on (22,80,443, 1000ms), arp cache.",
      "TCP port policy: tcp level-automatic level 3 (Recon): 100 ports (21..27018 …) [v1], timeout 800ms, concurrency 64, retries 1, mode requested=auto effective=connect.",
      "Service probe policy: service level 3 (recon): planner ≤6 probes/port, probe budget 2000ms, passive window 1000ms, speculative redis/postgres 800ms; unknown-port actives by level: L1 none, L2 http, L3 +redis, L4 +tls, L5 +postgres,smtp(220-gated); known ports append pivots at L4(+http)/L5(+redis,+tls).",
      "Web probe policy: web level 3 (Recon): method GET, redirects ≤2, connect 800ms, response 2000ms.",
      "Service fingerprinting: observed product/version strings derive vendor/CPE/version-family with calibrated confidence (exact version caps at 90 without corroboration, never above 95; port priors add zero); unknown services keep bounded correlation artifacts, never identity claims. External fingerprint packs under fingerprints/v1/*.json validate before load (malformed packs rejected, never crash); built-in evidence remains authoritative.",
      "Network intelligence (post-scan, passive, offline): OS candidates from fingerprints/os/v1 packs over banner/service evidence (passive-only; no active OS probes emitted; lone app hints capped at 65, multi-class required above 70, ceiling 90); device-role candidates from fingerprints/device/v1 packs (two signal kinds required, weak single-kind capped at 55, ceiling 90; vendor/model scored separately); SSH identity via banner parse + bounded Curve25519 KEX capture (no authentication; host keys become sshkey:sha256 entities for reuse/rotation tracking); TLS posture from handshake + certificate facts (deprecated protocol / expiry / mismatch / self-signed / short key / weak signature only when evidenced; no cipher enumeration by default); software inventory from service entities; offline vulnerability correlation from RXSCAN_VULN_DIR datasets (potential matches only, never verdicts; unknown versions indeterminate). Detail streams as os_candidate/device_candidate/ssh_host_key/tls_posture/software_identity/vulnerability_candidate/attention_event JSONL; project mode persists + diffs + assesses deterministically.",
      "Content discovery policy: content discovery level 3 (Recon): builtin 8, user-file false, request cap 32, candidate cap 64, body cap 65536.",
      "TCP scan mode: requested auto, resolved connect (auto selected connect: raw SYN unavailable: CAP_NET_RAW not available).",
      "Adaptive pacing: feedback-driven concurrency/timeout/ retry-delay suggestions stay within configured budgets; the scheduler remains authoritative and every adjustment is deterministic and explainable."
    ],
    "skipped": [
      "UdpDiscovery not selected by level 3 + workflow recon (no explicit request).",
      "Unsupported selected intents are skipped only when no real module is registered; skipped work is reported without fake discoveries.",
      "Current execution includes bounded host discovery (ICMP echo, TCP reachability, local ARP cache, interface/link-scope awareness), TCP port scanning with capability-gated syn/auto mode selection (raw SYN on capable Linux IPv4 hosts, connect otherwise; requested/effective/fallback always recorded), service probing (SSH/HTTP/TLS/FTP/SMTP/Redis/MySQL/PostgreSQL/SMB/RDP/MongoDB/MQTT/generic, no auth), DNS observations (A/AAAA/CNAME/MX/NS/TXT/PTR/SRV), HTTP/1.1 web observations with technology normalization, crawling, baseline checks, managed content discovery, inert contextual GET query fuzzing where evidence permits, plus passive post-scan intelligence (OS/device correlation, SSH identity, TLS posture, software inventory, offline vulnerability candidates, attention/change summaries in project mode) and per-entity project explain. Not implemented: raw SYN on IPv6 or non-Linux platforms, active OS-fingerprint probes, exhaustive cipher enumeration, SNMP authenticated polling, UPnP device-description fetching (SSDP stays classification-only; LOCATION never fetched), network-distance estimation beyond honest absence, password attacks / exploitation / destructive validation, JavaScript execution / browser automation, POST workflows, distributed scanning."
    ],
